From 1a69c6602d0cd858516db2d5ab91e0231ee44a84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Gamb <nick.gamb@solo.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:42:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): forward the user's OIDC ID token to agents in
 trusted-proxy mode

Some downstream flows need the signed-in user's identity assertion, not just
their access token. Cross App Access (draft-ietf-oauth-identity-assertion-authz-grant)
is the main one: the enterprise IdP issues an ID-JAG only for an ID token issued
to the requesting app. kagent is that app, but it forwards only Authorization and
X-User-Id to agents, so no agent can take part in XAA.

This adds optional ID token forwarding to the trusted-proxy authenticator:

- controller.auth.idToken.{header,cookie,audience} (AUTH_ID_TOKEN_HEADER /
  _COOKIE / _AUDIENCE): where the ID token arrives. The cookie form covers
  Envoy/kgateway OAuth2 filters (IdToken cookie).
- The token is forwarded to agents on A2A calls as X-Id-Token only when it is
  bound to the authenticated user: same `sub` as the access token, issued to
  `audience` (aud or azp), not expired. Anything else is dropped. It is never
  used to authenticate, so Authorization semantics are unchanged.
- Agents already forward allowed headers to MCP servers
  (tools[].mcpServer.allowedHeaders), so the ID token reaches only the tools
  that need it.

authConfig is a named type in cmd/controller; the auth mode tests use keyed
literals so new fields don't break them.
